keel-lnmp-19.0 (1) keel; urgency=low

  * The first release of Keel LNMP (handbook decision 0059): a layer on
    Keel Web with PHP-FPM 8.4 and MariaDB 11.8 from Debian 13. The
    appliance manifest lnmp.yaml (base web) declares MariaDB on 3306, a
    mesh port, PHP-FPM on its unix socket, the db_password secret and the
    db_user option, so a spec may declare the pair of 0049. The first boot
    hooks of the database come from keel-mariadb. The check page at
    /keel-check/ reads from MariaDB as www-data over the local socket,
    with SELECT on keel_check only.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000
